</section>
<!-- 4. CHAPTER 03 -->
<section class="ch" id="proof" aria-labelledby="comp-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="chap"><span class="chap-n">03</span> <span>Proof and trust</span></p>
    <div class="bento">
      <div class="bcell l" id="in-production">
        <span class="kicker">In production</span>
        <h2 id="prod-h">Zilogue runs on 10xGraph</h2>
        <p>Zilogue, the AI interview platform for hiring teams, runs on 10xGraph in production. It is built by 10xScale, the team that builds and maintains 10xGraph, so every release runs under real customer load before it ships.</p>
        <p class="center-link"><a href="https://www.zilogue.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit Zilogue<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span> &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="bcell r">
        <h2 id="comp-h">Built for teams going through SOC 2 and ISO 27001 audits</h2>
        <p>10xGraph is software you run, so the audit covers your organization and your deployment. The control mapping lists each SOC 2 and ISO 27001 control, the feature you can point to as evidence, and what stays yours.</p>
        <p class="center-link"><a href="/docs/production/control-mapping">Read the control mapping &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="bcell l">
        <h3>Evidence 10xGraph gives you</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Authentication and role-based access on every route</li>
          <li>Tenant isolation enforced in storage</li>
          <li>Rate limits and token revocation</li>
          <li>Security headers and production startup checks</li>
          <li>An audit log of access, denials and changes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bcell r">
        <h3>What stays with you</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Encryption at rest and backups</li>
          <li>Identity provider, MFA and access reviews</li>
          <li>Log retention and storage</li>
          <li>Network, TLS and secrets management</li>
          <li>Your organization's policies and processes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bcell f">
        <h2 id="p5h">Yours to run, on any model</h2>
        <p class="lede">MIT licensed, self-hosted, no LangChain dependency. Pick the provider with one model string; the graph, tools and endpoints stay the same.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bcell l">
        <h3>Good fit</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>You ship AI features to your own customers.</li>
          <li>You must self-host or keep data in your region.</li>
          <li>You need tenant isolation and access control from day one.</li>
          <li>Your team writes Python and wants code, not a builder.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bcell r">
        <h3>Not the right choice</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>You want a no-code builder.</b> 10xGraph is code-first Python.</li>
          <li><b>You want a hosted, managed service.</b> There is none; you run it.</li>
          <li><b>You need Python older than 3.12.</b></li>
          <li><b>You need the largest community and integration catalog.</b> LangGraph and CrewAI are bigger.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
